# Test: text fields keep a Win95 sunken edge when unfocused.
# Regression: unfocused fields rendered as flat white (no border at
# all) because text_input drops the bevel from its field config and
# skips its default border with a custom background; only the
# focused field showed an edge (upstream's black 2px border). The
# shared win95TextInput wrapper gives every dialog field a 1px
# sunken per-side edge (dark top/left, light bottom/right).
# Find auto-focuses its field on open, so focus is moved onto
# Find Next first to read the unfocused edge.

key CTRL+F
wait_frames 30

click_ui find_next
wait_frames 12
validate field_border_find_input=sunken
screenshot text_input_sunken_unfocused

focus_ui find_input
wait_frames 12
validate field_border_find_input=black
screenshot text_input_sunken_focused

escape
wait_frames 6
